The provider-neutral verb — the union of every provider's verbs, serde-tagged; the input half of the future subprocess plugin protocol. Each provider supports a subset and returns `UnsupportedVerb` for the rest.

```rust
#[serde(tag = "verb")]
enum ProviderCmd {
  Get          { id }
  Search       { entity?, query }
  Find         { entity, filters: [key:value] }
  Autocomplete { entity, q }
  CitedBy      { id }
  Refs         { id }
}
```

The provider seam: one dispatch over the neutral verb, returning the human half and the store half of every result in one pair.

```rust
trait Provider {
  fn name() -> &'static str
  fn dispatch(cmd: ProviderCmd, opts: &OutputOpts)
      -> Result<(Envelope, Emission), ProviderError>
}
```

impls: `OpenAlexProvider` · `ArxivProvider` · `SemanticScholarProvider`

crossref and opencitations do NOT implement it — they run a hand-rolled refs path in `main.rs`, pushing edges directly.
